# RNG-free CPU vs GPU correctness gate.
# Cold start + 0 thermalization + 0 sweeps-between => gauge field stays
# exactly identity (free field), NO RNG touched anywhere. Exercises the
# full fermion stack (Dirac op, even-odd, BiCGstab, 12-source propagator,
# meson contraction) deterministically. CPU and GPU must agree to CG tol.

-------------------------------
[Lattice]
-------------------------------
nX: 4
nY: 4
nZ: 4
nT: 8

-------------------------------
[Gauge Action]
-------------------------------
Beta: 6.0
Update Method: heatbath
Metropolis Epsilon: 0.2
Start Type: cold

-------------------------------
[Monte Carlo]
-------------------------------
Thermalization Sweeps: 0
Number of Configurations: 1
Sweeps Between Measurements: 0
Overrelaxation Sweeps: 0
Configuration Save Frequency: 10
Save Binary Configs: off
Random Seed: 42

-------------------------------
[Measurements]
-------------------------------
Measure Wilson Loops: off
Wilson Loop R Max: 2
Wilson Loop T Max: 2
Measure Polyakov: off
Measure Correlators: on
Verbose Output: on

-------------------------------
[Wilson Fermions]
-------------------------------
Kappa: 0.15
Wilson r: 1.0
CG Max Iterations: 2000
CG Tolerance: 1.0e-12
Solver Type: bicgstab

-------------------------------
[HMC]
-------------------------------
MD Steps: 20
MD Step Size: 0.01
HMC Trajectories: 100
